| `shell.excluded_paths.<path>` | string | none | an object, empty for none, each key a relative POSIX path (no leading or trailing `/`, no empty, `.` or `..` part) mapped to a non-blank reason | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.excluded_paths` row | Names a path, itself and everything under it by whole path parts, that no shell target judges, with the reason: a vendored script, which the house rule forbids editing to satisfy a linter. `vendor/lib` covers `vendor/lib/x.sh` and never `vendor/library.sh`. An entry that covers no file a commit could carry is exit 14 naming it, so an exclusion cannot outlive its file. A malformed entry is exit 14. The helper `make exit-codes-sh` generates, `scripts/exit_codes.sh`, needs no entry: `scripts/shell_gate.py` `HELPER_SH` keeps it from every shell target, because `make check-exit-codes` judges it. Absent, the targets write `[using default] shell.excluded_paths = {}` to stderr. | turning the shell gates off: `shell.enabled`; a project with no shell file: `shell.no_scripts` | always |
